Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-28-2020, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T20:39:15-07:00","id":1410936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403743-no-gods-no-masters-speculations?p=1410914#post1410914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, i remember those guys from 1st edition! <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayland_the_Smith\" target=\"_blank\">Wayland</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Himiko\" target=\"_blank\">Pimiko</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marinette_(Vodou)\" target=\"_blank\">Marinette</a> and - weird as it may sound - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hern%C3%A1n_Cort%C3%A9s\" target=\"_blank\">Hernan Cort\u00e9s</a> - were part of the cabal too, if memory tricks me not.<br /> They figured prominently though, not as core antagonists, in the one Scion saga i did ST (in parts, took turns at the chair with a friend) years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahahaha yeah uh, Cortez isn't a Keeper of the World this Edition. Nor is he a Scion at all, AFAIK. That's a particular bit of YIKES right there, implying that the Spanish conquest of the Aztec people had the divine backing of one of their Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T20:44:21-07:00","id":1410937,"title":"","content":"Yeah 1e was pretty yikes in general, I\u2019m curious to see what the full 2e lineup for them is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T20:48:52-07:00","id":1410938,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately I only know of a few. I THINK Wayland Smith may still be in the roster, I'm pretty sure Imhotep and Herakles are, I've heard rumors that Amergain and Karna are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T13:27:45-07:00","id":1411021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403743-no-gods-no-masters-speculations?p=1410936#post1410936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hahahaha yeah uh, Cortez isn't a Keeper of the World this Edition. Nor is he a Scion at all, AFAIK. That's a particular bit of YIKES right there, implying that the Spanish conquest of the Aztec people had the divine backing of one of their Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cortez had a weird context behind the idea for sure and i agree that it is a most contentious conceit the setting is better off without.<br /> Also, Amled might be a pretty good alternative as the Scion ambivalent/in denial/shock over its actual divine origin that could fit with the group.<br /> <br /> About a member for the group that would be an actual aztec mythic hero, unfortunately not my strong suite nor any suggestions at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-29-2020, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T19:45:35-07:00","id":1411041,"title":"","content":"Alas, i'm not as familiar as I'd like to be. I mean I personally don't think you need a representative from every Pantheon, just Enough To Be Interesting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T21:56:40-07:00","id":1411045,"title":"","content":"To be fair, there was only 6 pantheons at the time of 1st edition Keepers of the World were created. 6 is not a lot of people in a conspiracy to overthrow all the Gods in the World","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T23:23:15-07:00","id":1411047,"title":"","content":"But yes, if the rumors I heard are right and Amergain is in the Keepers, I'm curious to see how he'll be statted. Since well... As king of the Milisans I personally wouldn't stat him up as a God <i>exactly</i>, I'd make him a very powerful Saint more than anything. Given that in Origin, the Saints' main trick seems to be negation of Scale, and I hear they're getting new tricks in Saints and Monsters. This seems to fit the portrayal of the Milisans in the Book of Invasions, where they're skilled, yes, and all the powers of the Tuatha de don't seem to protect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T10:44:07-07:00","id":1411095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403743-no-gods-no-masters-speculations?p=1411045#post1411045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, there was only 6 pantheons at the time of 1st edition Keepers of the World were created. 6 is not a lot of people in a conspiracy to overthrow all the Gods in the World</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said upthread, I'm hoping that there will be more to 2e's version of the Keepers than just the \u201cone God per Pantheon\u201d that 1e featured. I'd like them to be, for lack of a better term, a \u201cpseudo-Pantheon\u201d of their own, with an alliance of disaffected Gods and Titans from various Pantheons heading things up but generally working through agents in the World to achieve their agenda. In some ways, I'd like to see this replace 1e's Order of the Divine Glory in the role of an organization of mortals who are antagonistic toward the gods \u2014 the difference being that they ironically have Divine patrons of their own (instead of somehow having enslaved a God), and they're not tied to the Abrahamic religions. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rather see Prometheus as a Keeper of the World than Herakles; but there's room for both, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T13:26:36-07:00","id":1411112,"title":"","content":"I think it's been mentioned Order of Divine Glory isn't off the table to appear in 2e, as Atenists trying to assimilate other gods under Aten - but they will in no way be implied to be the true face of all monotheist religions, as they were in 1e.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T13:35:03-07:00","id":1411113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403743-no-gods-no-masters-speculations?p=1410938#post1410938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately I only know of a few. I THINK Wayland Smith may still be in the roster, I'm pretty sure Imhotep and Herakles are, I've heard rumors that Amergain and Karna are?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, I think i have the list that was shared a bit ago...<br /> <br /> Imhotep, The One Who Comes in Peace (Netjeru)<br /> Herakles, God of Strength (Theoi)<br /> Karna, Between Dharma and Adharma (Deva)<br /> Dorje Shugden, the Enlightened Gyapo (Palas)<br /> Meng Po, the Old Lady (Shen)<br /> Takeminakata-no-Mikoto, Prince of the Earth (Kami)<br /> Tlazolteotl, Goddess of Filth and Purification (Teteo)<br /> Tolui Khagan, Odchigin Youngest Son, God of Family (Tengri)<br /> Wayland Smith (Aesir)<br /> Zalmoxis, God of Blood (solo deity of the Dacians)<br /> <br /> /Amergin [Irish Mythic figure who is emphatically not Tuatha De Danann] is involved as well, but as he is a Saint, not a God, he wasn't included is the above roster, who I believe are all getting Divine Parent/Patron writeups in Demigod/<br /> <br /> <br /> Gods who were asked but said no include Persephone, Confucius, Marienette, Savitar, and Amatsu-Mikaboshi","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-30-2020, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}